 return dict(applicable=True,scope='One original teaching guest or deterministic translation-cache model; synthetic markers only.',target='Original learner two-CPU address-space implementation with one deliberately premature frame-reuse path',environment='Disposable emulator guest with its own synthetic physical frames, or a clearly labeled deterministic cache model',attacker_capabilities='A teaching user task can repeatedly access its formerly mapped virtual address while the harness delays one CPU invalidation; it cannot target host memory or external systems.',isolation='Fresh VM, no host-disk/network/device passthrough, bounded execution and synthetic OLD/NEW markers; stop and discard the guest after each case.',defect='Reusing a physical frame while another CPU retains authority through a stale translation violates revocation and object isolation.',exposing_transition='Cache VA→A on CPU1, revoke its PTE on CPU0, withhold CPU1 invalidation, prematurely repurpose A, then access the old VA.',exploitability_limits='Requires a still-usable cached mapping, actual or modeled missing invalidation and premature reuse. A model violation is not hardware evidence; a crash or stale marker does not demonstrate arbitrary execution or privilege escalation.',success_condition='Only the original teaching target observes or modifies the synthetic NEW object through the revoked OLD mapping.',repair='Complete appropriate invalidation on every relevant CPU before reuse, with address-space membership, generation and acknowledgement ordering; retain frames on timeout.',regression='Compare flawed and repaired paths; delay one CPU, inject stale/duplicate acknowledgements, timeout, CPU membership changes and permission-revocation variants. The repaired target must never expose NEW through OLD.',residual_limits='Exact PCID/global-page/large-page and current CPU behavior require separate ISA inspection and target validation. The early retained IPI marker establishes only its narrower gate.')

